@startuml use-case-diagram-<package-slug>
' ============================================================
' UC-PACKAGE-<package-slug> — Use Case Package overview
'
' One overview diagram per UC package. The Product Owner owns this file
' and updates it whenever a UC is added, removed, or renamed in the package.
'
' ICONIX rules for use case package diagrams:
'   1. One package per diagram. The package boundary is explicit.
'   2. Every UC-XXX file in this package MUST appear here exactly once.
'   3. Every UC drawn here MUST have a matching `use-cases/UC-XXX-<slug>.md` file.
'   4. Cross-package use cases (those invoked from another package) appear OUTSIDE
'      the package rectangle, dashed, with a `<<include>>` or `<<extend>>` arrow.
'   5. Use case titles use noun-verb-noun and match the UC file title exactly.
'   6. Validated at M1: orphan UCs (file with no diagram entry) and ghost UCs
'      (diagram entry with no file) are M1-gate blockers.
'
' Relationship cheatsheet:
'   Actor   -->  UseCase                 association  (the actor participates)
'   UC-A    ..>  UC-B  : <<include>>     UC-A always invokes UC-B as part of itself
'   UC-A    <..  UC-B  : <<extend>>      UC-B is an optional extension of UC-A
'                                         (extends arrow points FROM the extension TO the base)
'   UC-A   --|>  UC-B                    generalisation (UC-A is a kind of UC-B)
' ============================================================

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #FEFEFE
  BorderColor #444444
}
skinparam shadowing false

' ── Actors ────────────────────────────────────────────────
actor "<Primary actor>"   as Actor1
actor "<Secondary actor>" as Actor2

' ── Package boundary (one and only one rectangle) ─────────
rectangle "<Package name> package" as Pkg {
  usecase "<UC title>\n(<PREFIX>-UC-XXX)" as UC1
  usecase "<UC title>\n(<PREFIX>-UC-YYY)" as UC2
  usecase "<UC title>\n(<PREFIX>-UC-ZZZ)" as UC3
}

' ── Cross-package use cases (outside the rectangle) ──────
usecase "<UC title>\n(<PREFIX>-UC-NNN, <other-package> package)" as UCExt

' ── Actor associations ────────────────────────────────────
Actor1 --> UC1
Actor1 --> UC2
Actor2 --> UC3

' ── Use-case relationships ────────────────────────────────
UC1 ..> UCExt : <<include>>
UC2 <.. UC3   : <<extend>>

note bottom of Pkg
  Maintenance reminder:
  - When you add a new UC-XXX file to this package, add a `usecase` line above.
  - When you rename a UC, rename it both here and in the file (M1 will reject mismatches).
  - When you split a UC, replace its line with the new UC-IDs.
end note

@enduml
